#question(title: [Functions, inverses, and graphs])[
  Sketch the graph of a function $g$
  satisfying all the following properties:

  + The domain of $g$ is $RR$.
  + $g$ is continuous everywhere except at
    $-2$.
  + $g$ is differentiable everywhere except
    at $-2$ and $1$.
  + $g$ has an inverse function.
  + $g(0) = 2$
  + $g' (0) = 2$
  + $display((g^(-1))' (- 3) = - 2)$.
]
